ready: 1
kind: rule
id: capture.rule.classify
display_id: RULE-CAPTURE-CLASSIFY
module: capture
title: What a session record becomes
summary: Each record in a runtime session becomes an event of one kind with an actor and a trust tier, or is dropped.
decision:
  nodes:
    - {id: in, node_kind: input, text: "One parsed record; for Claude Code the role and content blocks are read from inside its message"}
    - {id: own, node_kind: decision, text: "Did Kernle produce it (marked injected context, a Kernle hook attachment, a Kernle tool call or result, or a session Kernle ran for its own model work)?", refs: [capture.const.injection-marker]}
    - {id: book, node_kind: decision, text: Is it runtime bookkeeping such as file snapshots or progress ticks?}
    - {id: user, node_kind: decision, text: "Is it text the person typed, not a tool result or system text?"}
    - {id: intr, node_kind: decision, text: Is it the person interrupting?}
    - {id: asst, node_kind: decision, text: Is it the agent's visible text?}
    - {id: think, node_kind: decision, text: Is it the agent's private reasoning?}
    - {id: call, node_kind: decision, text: Is it a tool call?}
    - {id: res, node_kind: decision, text: Is it a tool result?}
    - {id: write, node_kind: decision, text: Did the tool write a file the agent asked it to write?}
    - {id: cmp, node_kind: decision, text: Is it a compaction summary?}
    - {id: ses, node_kind: decision, text: Is it session start or end information?}
    - {id: drop, node_kind: outcome, text: Dropped and not stored}
    - {id: e_user, node_kind: outcome, text: A person's message from the principal}
    - {id: e_int, node_kind: outcome, text: An interrupt from the principal}
    - {id: e_ast, node_kind: outcome, text: "An agent message, agent-inferred"}
    - {id: e_call, node_kind: outcome, text: "A tool call, first-party"}
    - {id: e_status, node_kind: outcome, text: "A tool status, first-party: success or error, exit code, duration, test counts when readable"}
    - {id: e_out1, node_kind: outcome, text: "Tool output confirming the agent's own write, first-party"}
    - {id: e_out3, node_kind: outcome, text: "Tool output, third-party: file reads, shell output, web pages, and results from other tools"}
    - {id: e_cmp, node_kind: outcome, text: "A compaction summary, agent-inferred"}
    - {id: e_ses, node_kind: outcome, text: "A session start or end, first-party"}
    - {id: unk, node_kind: outcome, text: Dropped and counted as a parse error}
  edges:
    - {from: in, to: own}
    - {from: own, to: drop, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: own, to: book, label: "No"}
    - {from: book, to: drop, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: book, to: user, label: "No"}
    - {from: user, to: e_user, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: user, to: intr, label: "No"}
    - {from: intr, to: e_int, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: intr, to: asst, label: "No"}
    - {from: asst, to: e_ast, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: asst, to: think, label: "No"}
    - {from: think, to: drop, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: think, to: call, label: "No"}
    - {from: call, to: e_call, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: call, to: res, label: "No"}
    - {from: res, to: e_status, label: "Yes, first of two events"}
    - {from: res, to: write, label: "Yes, second of two events"}
    - {from: write, to: e_out1, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: write, to: e_out3, label: "No"}
    - {from: res, to: cmp, label: "No"}
    - {from: cmp, to: e_cmp, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: cmp, to: ses, label: "No"}
    - {from: ses, to: e_ses, label: "Yes"}
    - {from: ses, to: unk, label: "No"}
rules:
  - trust.rule.source-tier
rationale: >-
  A tool result becomes two events because whether a command succeeded is something the agent
  observed, while what a file or page printed may have been written by anyone. Lessons grounded in
  success or failure can then apply on their own, while claims that rest only on outside text are
  held. Kernle's own output is dropped first so a recalled memory is never captured as new
  experience and strengthened in a loop. Private reasoning is dropped because it is often redacted
  and storing it adds exposure without helping appraisal.
